}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-05-18T00:56:50Z","updated_at":"2016-05-18T00:56:50Z","body":"I think I have a fix for this, but it's late and I'll have to continue after having a good sleep :smile: I want to add a few more tricky test cases, but my brain is fried rn.\n\nBy the way, just to make sure: should this be ok with `object-property-newline` turned on?\n\n``` js\nvar obj = { k1: 'val1', [\n  k2]: 'val2' };\n```\n\nCurrently there's no error thrown for that and I think that's wrong, because the second property starts at the first line.\n\nAlso this case, with `allowMultiplePropertiesPerLine: true`:\n\n``` js\nvar obj = { [\n  k1]: 'val1', k2: 'val2' };\n```\n\nNo error here too, while the first property starts at the first line.\n\nMy fix would take such cases into consideration too.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/219897227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"fatfisz","id":6004414,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDQ0MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6004414?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz","html_url":"https://github.com/fatfisz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatfisz/gists{/gist_i